unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7059006","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4bad04d00c5d58fa935d08ff50040d000aeb815e106ed921b9fae21a058f4963","compact":"3e52bd3d11e12025ebf55ff98e4d212a237e708f851915f517ba03358383513c","nasal":"030b488d3ffae6e43cf946556ef8d24330b5ef647eff5dcac5a7fa97ceb8a257"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-59-7","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":59,"verse":7,"english":"He having been engaged in making preparations to conquer the world of gods—the celestial chief Indra with other immortals was greatly terrified.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.587,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-67-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7059007","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f7273776fc466b7e4fcece341c2bdcfb1b5ff1bd9f2e73719fb66f94576a5f07","compact":"87cebb486e9088b20d3fc340f6f443f3f81479cbe0ca69300e88a30779dc7dcb","nasal":"595ac9cb4da31513bca96c8f3bcfe79ac442185c5d79a78de0d9c075fa33583b"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-59-8","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":59,"verse":8,"english":"With this promise, the king Mândhāta went into the celestial region that he would occupy the half of Indra's throne and kingdom and the celestials would adore him. Being apprised of this vicious intention of his, Indra, the slayer of Pāka, consoled him in sweet words, saying.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-67-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7059008","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7ab0414429ca7a44b21c76aa78143c548de8efa3823aeaff019aa3822ca4722a","compact":"adb402cf24e15431b26b12e4717e6167e0677f685d4f3f4c28275eef736d45b8","nasal":"f05367931e8798f6e85f32536fe02e0e824b2b8e9c96457eea708d9833fcaa2f"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-59-9","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":59,"verse":9,"english":"With this promise, the king Mândhāta went into the celestial region that he would occupy the half of Indra's throne and kingdom and the celestials would adore him. Being apprised of this vicious intention of his, Indra, the slayer of Pāka, consoled him in sweet words, saying.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-67-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7059009","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cdba5a7ffd7279a79eaeb614dc447df45b86c09a23f7adc1ef5cd2ec18117b6e","compact":"095e2e486e2ff5e5619f80ceecaa2da2ffad967de69fb2b6f4475c1397b17354","nasal":"0287297fe3616bcc3534a9de924f184a20538062be384a650c54bc11bec44b59"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-59-10","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":59,"verse":10,"english":"O foremost of men, even in the land of men, you have not been able to become the real king. Without perfectly subjugating the earth how do you wish to lord over the celestial kingdom?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-67-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7059010","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8d8d36d22f480788eebbf984795bcbab138fed3e95cda9bd735dd7bd906e9450","compact":"c1f45be9df277b70ace7c3776779173041211c11920f0cb35a037dd79b7e897d","nasal":"c1f45be9df277b70ace7c3776779173041211c11920f0cb35a037dd79b7e897d"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-59-11","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":59,"verse":11,"english":"If the whole world is under your subjection, O hero, be you, with the whole host of your servants and soldiers, installed on the celestial throne.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-67-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7059011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit