assador, having gone there, addressed many unpleasant words to Lavaņa and the nightranger devoured him.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-67-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7059017","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8f09986318242b8a6da017aa70e7be0a2ccf3103a38498e35e479dfc57c2a429","compact":"bc6a42551410c19b582cf395683a01f43afb3edc67b6a9629a45b0473734cf86","nasal":"ccea7925b44db3467c210e03cc7102da0f4e51875bad741a0b44d9f15a0dd835"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-59-18","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":59,"verse":18,"english":"The ambassador, having gone there, addressed many unpleasant words to Lavaņa and the nightranger devoured him.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-67-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7059018","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9af1f10ab193201471ec281af0e0c91fca6062604906ce952b7c6b90cb42f982","compact":"48cc56d4e1ba60bdbe35aec09eebd64e77829e2c13f7457a752acaa478eac68f","nasal":"1cd1ae12ead76fc1f82f2bf6d40b5ef392b82856a3491290e5898f684d7872b1"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-59-19","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":59,"verse":19,"english":"On the other hand finding the delay of his return the king Māndhāta, enraged, began to assail the Raksasa Lavaņa with arrows from all sides.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-67-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7059019","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5f96cf517e4cf9b6e7063b9219bd44f6ab09e88a1c9a2859d4f21fd2526ca102","compact":"2bd13337c7b6f1e8e816481d31be4854d439c4a784426dc2ec38c467c55dc902","nasal":"c11795cfb1662747884b5983fa01d128050c950547a667d71811fedf14957d0e"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-59-20","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":59,"verse":20,"english":"Laughing wild Lavaņa took up the dart in his hand and discharged it to destroy the king with his followers.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.818,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-67-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7059020","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"25a7fbe879cd958704ea217d8d39da833563565357ce094caff5b7358d0a0ac4","compact":"320b2144166481fb4ea97035c4ef135a528b2772f61dfb7b1406dd2c636e4226","nasal":"4a538f33453d761f262d1d0966db3f3426625825382f9dffc60b3468af32d77a"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-59-21","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":59,"verse":21,"english":"Thereupon growing powerful the dart reduced the king with his servants and army into ashes and returned to Lavaņa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.724,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-67-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7059021","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"81e8f0b3b2837cb738e4c0752c187d9a37dd17a4c7970936cb3ef4249b56c281","compact":"99c62b024748bc276ae18567ecec640d80a4c56ab14ebb01ddea56388d492a9c","nasal":"7b4d992f9949cea9b3fe05ffdfbac750673b4f7fe82b6edd093c4930243366e8"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-59-22","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":59,"verse":22,"english":"In this wise the high-souled king Māndhāta, with his huge army, was slain. O gentle hero, incomparable and great is the strength of the dart..","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.708,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-67-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7059022","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1f308d60f6fbdf6adcfaa46c6bbd1dc9ccb7e222dca5e3038e5f901f4227cb77","compact":"24a176718ea00a3e4cfc83dd04c19b99b72029dbf066810aaf6dfe47d5f36575","nasal":